  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis and on the origin respectively.</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> will lie on circle whose diameter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ca769eba-dd0c-45da-9182-749577dd8be4.png\" style=\"width: 205px; height: 165px;\"/></p><p>Equation of the circle will be given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>13</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>",
